# Naming Conventions

Use Rails idioms first, domain language second, and invent nothing. Boring, obvious names are correct; clever names are a smell. When Rails convention and domain language conflict, **Rails convention wins for class and file names**; **domain language wins for method and variable names**.

A name says what the thing does, and only that thing: when a shorter name leaves two readings, take the longer, specific one (`SetCurrentRequestDetails` over `SetRequest`, `approver_id` over `user_id`).

## Suffixes and Casing

- **Add:** `Controller`, `Job`, `Mailer`, `Policy`, `Scope` (Pundit), `_spec`, `_path`
- **Never add:** `Model`, `Class`, `Manager`, `Handler`, `Helper` (on non-helpers), `Service`
- **Singular vs plural:** models, form objects, and factory symbols are singular (`factory :article`); controllers and tables are plural; factory files take the plural (`spec/factories/articles.rb`)
- **Casing:** classes PascalCase, methods and columns snake_case, constants SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE, Stimulus identifiers kebab-case

## Domain Layer (Models, Concerns, POROs)

| Thing | Convention | Examples |
|-------|-----------|----------|
| Model | Singular PascalCase noun | `Article`, `User`, `ProjectMembership` |
| Concern | `-able` adjective of the domain verb — § Concerns | `Publishable`, `Closeable`, `Card::Closeable` |
| Scope | Business term or adverb | `chronologically`, `active`, `preloaded`, `recent` |
| State record | Noun for the state | `Closure`, `Publication`, `Archival`, `Lock` |
| Domain verb | Imperative, non-bang | `publish`, `close`, `archive`, `gild`, `invite` |
| Predicate method | Present tense + `?` | `published?`, `closed?`, `member?`, `locked?` |
| Bang domain verb | Only when a "try" form also exists | `lock!` alongside `lock` — not a default suffix |
| PORO under model | Namespaced PascalCase noun | `Article::Publisher`, `Account::Onboarding` |
| Form object | Standalone domain noun | `Registration`, `Invitation`, `ArticleTransfer` |

Do **not** use generic CRUD verbs as domain names: `set_status`, `update_flag`, `create_record`. The name should reflect what happens in the domain, not which SQL call fires underneath.

Default to non-bang for domain verbs — they are the normal path and propagate exceptions from inner `create!` / `update!` naturally. Add a bang only when you also offer a non-raising alternative (`lock` returns false on failure; `lock!` raises).

## Concerns

`app/models/concerns`, `app/controllers/concerns`, and `app/policies/concerns` are all autoload roots, so every concern shares one constant namespace: a `Searchable` under models and a `Searchable` under controllers cannot coexist, and nothing in the bare name says which layer it belongs to. Each layer has its own shape, and the shape names the layer.

| Layer | Shape | The name says | Examples |
|-------|-------|---------------|----------|
| Model concern shared by two or more models | `-able` adjective of the domain verb, in `app/models/concerns/` | what any includer can do | `Publishable`, `Archivable`, `Taggable` |
| Model concern decomposing one model | The same adjective namespaced under that model, in `app/models/card/closeable.rb` | the one model it belongs to | `Card::Closeable`, `Article::Publishable` |
| Controller concern loading a parent resource for a nested family | `{Parent}Scoped` | which parent its `before_action` loads | `BoardScoped` sets `@board`, `AccountScoped` sets `@account` |
| Controller concern running one `before_action` on every request | `Set{Detail}` — the callback method, PascalCased | what every request gets | `SetCurrentRequestDetails`, `SetLocale`, `SetPlatform` |
| Controller concern adding a mechanism with helpers and callbacks | Noun for the mechanism | what the controller gains | `Authentication`, `Authorization` |
| Policy concern shared by some policies, not all | `{Role}Permissions`, in `app/policies/concerns/` | which role's permissions and predicates it carries | `OwnerPermissions`, `AccountMemberPermissions` |

A model concern's adjective shares its stem with everything it provides: `Publishable` gives `publish`, `published?`, the `published` scope, and the `Publication` state record. A concern whose verb has a different stem (`Publishable` providing `release`) has misnamed one or the other.

A policy concern is rare. A predicate every policy needs lives on `ApplicationPolicy`, tenant scoping on `ApplicationPolicy::Scope`, and a predicate one policy needs is a private method on that policy (`agent_harness_rails/rules/policies.mdc`). Extract only when several policies, but not all, grant one role the same actions.

Never: a bare adjective on a controller or policy concern (that shape is the model layer's), a `Has` prefix, a bare gerund (`Publishing`), or a `Concern`, `Behavior`, `Module`, or `Helper` suffix.

## Controllers

| Thing | Convention | Examples |
|-------|-----------|----------|
| Resource controller | Plural PascalCase + `Controller` | `ArticlesController`, `ProjectMembershipsController` |
| Singleton resource controller | Still plural — `resource :x` routes to the plural controller | `resource :session` → `SessionsController`, `resource :account` → `AccountsController` |
| Namespaced | Module-prefixed | `Admin::ArticlesController`, `Api::V1::UsersController` |
| Action names | Seven standard REST actions only | `index`, `show`, `new`, `create`, `edit`, `update`, `destroy` |

A non-REST action name is a signal to extract a new resource. `publish` on `ArticlesController` should be `create` on `PublicationsController`.

## Views and Partials

| Thing | Convention | Examples |
|-------|-----------|----------|
| View template | Matches controller + action | `app/views/articles/show.html.erb` |
| Partial | Underscore prefix, singular noun | `_article.html.erb`, `_form.html.erb`, `_header.html.erb` |
| Layout | Lowercase, semantic | `application`, `admin`, `minimal` |
| Local variable in partial | Singular domain noun | `article`, `user`, `membership` — not `item`, `obj`, `record` |
| Stimulus controller identifier | Kebab-case, mirrors DOM scope | `article-form`, `inline-editor`, `dropdown` |

## Jobs

| Thing | Convention | Examples |
|-------|-----------|----------|
| Job class | `{Verb}{Noun}Job` | `NotifySubscribersJob`, `CleanupExpiredSessionsJob`, `SyncInventoryJob` |
| Perform method | Always `perform` | Never rename — it is the ActiveJob contract |

Verb first so jobs sort by action: `Deliver*`, `Notify*`, `Sync*`, `Process*`. The noun names what is acted on.

## Mailers

| Thing | Convention | Examples |
|-------|-----------|----------|
| Mailer class | `{Noun}Mailer` | `UserMailer`, `InvitationMailer`, `OrderMailer` |
| Mailer method | Domain event or action | `welcome`, `invitation`, `password_reset`, `receipt` |

## Policies (Pundit)

| Thing | Convention | Examples |
|-------|-----------|----------|
| Policy class | Matches model + `Policy` | `ArticlePolicy`, `ProjectMembershipPolicy` |
| Scope | Nested `Scope` class | `ArticlePolicy::Scope` |
| Permission methods | CRUD action + `?` only | `show?`, `update?`, `destroy?` — no custom verbs |
| State-change policy | Noun-resource namespace | `Articles::PublicationPolicy`, `Cards::ClosurePolicy` |

No custom verb methods (`publish?`, `close?`) — state changes are CRUD on a
noun-resource policy (`Articles::PublicationPolicy#create?`), mirroring the
controller mapping. See `agent_harness_rails/rules/policies.mdc`.

## Database

| Thing | Convention | Examples |
|-------|-----------|----------|
| Table | Plural snake_case | `articles`, `project_memberships`, `publication_locks` |
| Column | Snake_case, semantic | `published_at`, `creator_id`, `locked_reason` |
| Datetime column | `_at` suffix | `published_at`, `closed_at`, `expires_at` |
| Date-only column | `_on` suffix | `due_on`, `starts_on`, `expires_on` |
| Boolean column | Adjective, no `is_` prefix | `active`, `featured`, `locked` — not `is_active` |
| Foreign key | `{singular_model}_id` — use semantic name when role differs from class | `creator_id` (User), `approver_id` (User) — not `user_id` when the role is specific |
| Join table | Alphabetical order, no surrogate key | `articles_tags`, `memberships_roles` |
| Migration file | Descriptive verb phrase | `add_published_at_to_articles`, `create_project_memberships`, `remove_legacy_status_from_users` |

Avoid grab-bag column names: `data`, `info`, `details`. `type` is reserved
for Rails STI. A single obvious lifecycle enum may be called `status` (the
models rule uses exactly that); name the axis (`publication_state`,
`review_stage`) as soon as a second lifecycle dimension appears.

## Routes and Helpers

| Thing | Convention | Examples |
|-------|-----------|----------|
| Resource | Plural noun | `resources :articles` |
| Singleton resource | Singular noun | `resource :session`, `resource :account` |
| Path helper | `{resource}_path` / `{resource}_url` | `article_path`, `new_project_membership_path` |
| Namespace | Lowercase singular | `namespace :admin`, `namespace :api` |
| Custom route | Rare, honest, commented | Always prefer a new resource noun over a custom verb segment |

## Tests and Factories

| Thing | Convention | Examples |
|-------|-----------|----------|
| Spec file | Mirrors app path + `_spec` suffix | `spec/models/article_spec.rb`, `spec/system/publishing_spec.rb` |
| Factory name | Matches model name (singular symbol) | `:article`, `:project_membership` |
| Factory trait | Domain adjective or past participle | `:published`, `:closed`, `:with_members`, `:as_admin` |
| `let` / `let!` | Meaningful domain noun | `let(:article)`, `let(:author)` — not `let(:obj)` or `let(:user1)` |
| `describe` block | Class name or `#method` / `.class_method` | `describe Article`, `describe "#publish"`, `describe ".active"` |
| `context` block | `"when …"` or `"with …"` | `context "when published"`, `context "with no members"` |
| `it` block | Third-person present, no "should" | `"creates a publication record"`, `"raises when already closed"` |

Use role names, not ordinals: `author`, `reviewer`, `admin` — not `user1`, `user2`.

## Variables and Locals

- **Full words** — `article` not `a`, `membership` not `m`.
- **Domain nouns for instances** — `user`, `account`, `article` — not `record`, `object`, `item`, `thing`.
- **Plural for collections** — `articles`, `memberships` — not `article_list` or `arr`.
- **No Hungarian notation** — no `strName`, `bActive`, `arrItems`.
- **Block parameters match the domain noun** — `articles.each { |article| }` not `{ |a| }`.
- **Meaningful boolean locals** — `published`, `locked` — not `flag`, `result`, `ok`.

## Anti-Patterns

| Anti-Pattern | Correct |
|-------------|---------|
| `set_status`, `update_flag`, `do_publish` | Domain verb: `close`, `publish`, `archive` |
| `ArticleModel`, `UserClass` | `Article`, `User` — no suffix Rails doesn't expect |
| `ArticleManager`, `UserHandler` | Model methods or namespaced PORO |
| `PublishingConcern`, `TaggingBehavior`, `HasPublication` | Adjective of the verb: `Publishable`, `Taggable` |
| `Searchable`, `Sortable` as controller concerns | Query belongs in a model scope; a controller concern is `{Parent}Scoped`, `Set{Detail}`, or a mechanism noun |
| `AccountScoped` as a policy concern | `AccountMemberPermissions` — the `Scoped` shape is a controller's |
| `ArticleService`, `PublishService` | Model domain verb — see `agent_harness_rails/rules/services.mdc` |
| `is_active`, `is_locked`, `has_members` | `active`, `locked`, `member?` |
| `created_date`, `updated_time` | `created_at`, `updated_at` — Rails timestamps |
| `tags_articles` join table | Alphabetical: `articles_tags` |
| Grab-bag column: `data`, `info`, `misc` | Semantic: `settings`, `bio`, `preferences` |
| One `status` column serving two lifecycles | Name each axis: `publication_state`, `review_stage` |
| `execute`, `run`, `do` on POROs | Domain verb: `complete`, `transfer`, `process` |
| `user1`, `user2` in specs | Role names: `author`, `reviewer`, `admin` |
| `it "should create…"` | `it "creates…"` — no "should" |
| `describe "testing publish"` | `describe "#publish"` |
